### A.7: Protected Route Group Layouts
**Goal:** Add server-side auth gates to route groups so unauthorized users are blocked before any page code runs.

**Current State — route groups exist but have NO layout guards:**
- `(admin)/` — org-dashboard, faq-management — **no auth**
- `(dpo)/` — investigator page — **no auth**
- `(staff)/` — dashboard — only middleware `/dashboard` prefix check

**Changes:**
1. **[NEW]** `src/app/(admin)/layout.tsx`:
   ```typescript
   import { requireRole } from '@/lib/auth-guard'
   export default async function AdminLayout({ children }) {
       await requireRole(['Admin', 'Medical Superintendent'])
       return <>{children}</>
   }
   ```
2. **[NEW]** `src/app/(dpo)/layout.tsx`:
   ```typescript
   import { requirePrivileged } from '@/lib/auth-guard'
   export default async function DPOLayout({ children }) {
       await requirePrivileged(['DPO', 'Admin'])
       return <>{children}</>
   }
   ```
3. **[NEW]** `src/app/(staff)/layout.tsx`:
   ```typescript
   import { requireUser } from '@/lib/auth-guard'
   export default async function StaffLayout({ children }) {
       await requireUser()
       return <>{children}</>
   }
   ```

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Navigating to `/org-dashboard` without Admin role → error/redirect
- [ ] Navigating to `/investigator` without DPO role + MFA → error/redirect
- [ ] Deactivated staff cannot access any staff pages

